1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,500
Graduate School staff signs in.

2
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:18,100
Reports and Analytics, under Overview. Filters on top: program, entry cohort and period. Below, the six numbers the office asks about most.

3
00:00:18,399 --> 00:00:23,400
Behind schedule: the share of active students who are behind, against a target.

4
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:29,600
Median days to decide, against the twelve months before. Every number is computed from recorded events.

5
00:00:30,199 --> 00:00:36,199
Needs attention. Each bar is a cause; the longest affects the most students.

6
00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:41,199
Selecting a cause narrows the list to the students affected.

7
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:50,399
Show all causes restores the list, most delayed first, with the office that can move each student on. Download it as Excel or PDF.

8
00:00:51,799 --> 00:00:57,699
Where students get stuck counts students per stage as on time, slow or stuck.

9
00:00:57,899 --> 00:01:03,099
Every count is a button that opens the real students behind it.

10
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:11,599
Office speed: which offices take longest to close requests. The longest red bar marks the office to ask first.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,799
Records to fix lists research students with missing records, such as no adviser. A fixed record drops off.

12
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,399
Cohorts by stage.

13
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:27,200
Graduation candidates: who can graduate and what is missing.

14
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,500
Overdue and pending: each waiting task, longest first.

15
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:35,899
Defenses held and upcoming, with panel and verdict.

16
00:01:37,299 --> 00:01:41,399
Registrar changes: the daily list the Registrar must apply in AIMS.

17
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:50,099
Every filter covers the whole page. One program picked, and all the numbers follow.
